    26	## Artifact Health Values
    27	
    28	- `valid`: evidence exists, is fresh enough, and can be cited.
    29	- `stale`: evidence exists but violates freshness or drift rules.
    30	- `missing`: evidence path or source is absent.
    31	- `inconclusive`: evidence exists but cannot support acceptance.
    32	- `blocked`: evidence requires human access or external setup.
    33	
    34	## Claim Support Values
    35	
    36	- `supports`: supports the claim being tested.
    37	- `refutes`: refutes the claim being tested.
    38	- `partial`: supports only part of the claim.
    39	- `unrelated`: valid artifact but not relevant to the claim.
    40	- `unknown`: claim relationship has not been assessed.
    41	
    42	## Acceptance Effect Values
    43	
    44	- `pass`: contributes to accepting a round.
    45	- `fail`: contributes to rejecting a round.
    46	- `neutral`: cited but not decisive.
    47	- `blocked`: cannot be evaluated without access or human action.
    48	
    49	## Evidence Types
    50	
    51	- static
    52	- dynamic
    53	- runtime
    54	- source
    55	- human-confirmation
