harnessloop/plugins/harnessloop/skills/harnessloop-loop/SKILL.md:204:`$harnessloop-channels` lists all declared external systems, channels, and tools without probing. `$harnessloop-connectivity` checks only declared connectivity methods and must ask the user before any missing condition, parameter, credential reference, permission, write target, or named tool is inferred. Treat `harnessloop:channels` and `harnessloop:connectivity` as natural-language aliases. If connectivity self-check returns `fail`, `blocked`, `skipped`, or `needs-user-confirmation` because required information is missing or invalid, ask the user for the exact missing information before continuing the loop.
